\f0\fs24 \cf0 # zerOm Intro\
\
## Meeting Info\
- Attendees: Saurabh Verma, Lavi Sahu, Prabhat Agarwal, Ravi Shanker\
\
## Summary\
### Flow Summary\
zerOm walked through their causal decision engine axon. and a personalized promotions demo built on UAE retailer Union Coop data. Feedback focused on trust, transparency, MECE KPI signals, edge cases, and surfacing positives alongside pain points.\
\
### Team & Context\
\
- zerOm relocating base to Dubai next Monday/Tuesday to build client base there\
- Saurabh has left ADA, joined full-time; now three co-founders (Ravi, Saurabh, + Speaker 3)\
\
### zerOm / axon. Pitch\
\
- Vision: democratize trusted enterprise intelligence at scale via unified causal engine (not correlation)\
- Positioned as next Palantir for growth & ops; references Bengio, LeCun, Judea Pearl\
- axon. builds unified enterprise causal graph, not knowledge graph; capabilities: detect, explain, recommend, simulate, act\
\
### Demo: Union Coop Personalized Promotions\
\
- Data: 4 stores, 1500 txns/day for 2 years, transaction-level, revenue \\~2.2B dirhams\
    - Cohort-level customer data; DAG built with cycles/substitution/cannibalization handled\
- CMO cockpit shows signals (margin down 5.6%), recommendations re-allocate promo budget across categories\
    - LLM used only for intent parsing & tool selection; deterministic tools do calculations\
\
### Feedback from Speaker 1\
\
- KPIs shown as 'needs attention' should be MECE and clearly distinct to avoid dispute\
- Surface positives too, not only pain points; give holistic view across sub-personas\
- Causal linkage must land smoothly; explainability/trust is the crux, cover edge cases not happy flow\
- Caution on LLM world-knowledge assumptions (e.g. perishables stockpiling) \'97 may fail in specific industries\
\
### Next Steps\
\
- (Speaker 1) Send Andrew Ng video on simplifying many-to-many causal graphs into simple flows\
- (Speaker 3) Rework summary view to show both what's on-track and what needs attention (holistic view)\
- (Speaker 3) Design tabular representation of causal graph alongside visual, for simpler consumption\
- (Speaker 3) Add provision for users to feed corrections/business knowledge back into the system to override LLM assumptions\
- (Speaker 3) Build backtesting view showing lift on past data using same formulas to build trust\
\
### Decisions Made\
\
- zerOm base shifting to Dubai next week\
- LLM restricted to intent parsing and tool selection; all calculations via in-house deterministic tools\
\
